 affected failure arm (HTTP error, malformed-response rejection, cursor stall), the disposition it surfaces to the caller using an explicit disposition word (retryable/transient vs fatal/permanent).","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'Reject malformed search responses; invalidate a partially failed search so a later attempt cannot silently reuse a truncated result.'","Plan quote: 'HTTP/malformed-response failure and retry without partial-cache poisoning' — implies a retry arm but no disposition word is attached to any arm.","ABSENCE: no explicit transient/retryable vs fatal/permanent classification is stated for HTTP failure, malformed-response, or cursor-stall arms."],"finding":"The plan alters failure/exception/retry semantics on the search path (reject malformed responses, invalidate on partial failure, retry) but never states, per affected arm, the disposition the caller surfaces using an explicit disposition word (retryable/transient vs fatal/permanent). It is unspecified whether an HTTP error, a malformed-response rejection, or a cursor stall surfaces as transient/retryable versus fatal/permanent to the fetcher.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fae5f3f980c21e254","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach: 'Reject malformed search responses; invalidate a partially failed search...' and Testing: 'HTTP/malformed-response failure and retry without partial-cache poisoning'","norm_id":"nfa846f8c5c452ed1","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A transient HTTP 429/503 mid-pagination could be surfaced as a permanent failure (or vice versa), changing whether the bridge run retries or alarms — the same class of masking that motivates stating disposition per arm."],"severity":null,"sug