n found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how the preserved (jql, start_at, max_results) signature maps onto the forward-only opaque cursor — e.g. the per-JQL memo accumulates fetched pages so arbitrary/backward/repeated start_at slices are served from memory while only forward cursor exhaustion issues network pages — and confirm this does not misfire _iter_pages' startAt offset-stall or next_page_token same-token-twice guards.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5906,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["acli_graph.py:283-289 — '/rest/api/3/search/jql ... there is NO total field and sending startAt is rejected with HTTP 400 ... paginates via an opaque nextPageToken cursor'","fetch_paging.py:117-217 — the driver advances by `start_at += len(page)` and runs offset-stall (first_key repeat at new offset) + same-token-twice detection keyed on a client next_page_token/nextPageToken attribute","acli.py:426-481 — current search_issues is stateless (slices a per-JQL list); a stateful cursor walker changes this invariant, and the client currently exposes no next_page_token attribute (search returned no matches)","ABSENCE: the plan gestures at 'out-of-order slice calls' and 'cursor stall' testing but does not state the mechanism (memo-serves-slices vs forward-only-cursor-advance) that makes a backward/repeated start_at safe and keeps _iter_pages' guards from misfiring on the new stateful client"],"finding":"The plan preserves search_issues(jql, start_at, max_results) over a forward-only opaque-cursor endpoint, but does not state how arbitrary/out-of-order/backward start_at requests are reconciled with a cursor that cannot seek (the endpoint rejects startAt with HTTP 400 and exposes no total), given that the fetcher driver _iter_pages advances via `start_at += len(page)` and also runs startAt-based offset-stall and token-attribute same-token-twice guards against the client.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f87405891f0e5dab6","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section: 'Preserve search_issues(jql,start_at,max_results)...Keep cursor progress checked before emitting a stalled page'","norm_id":"n42700c9f45551517","priority":0.2094,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reconcile pass or retry re-requests an earlier start_at slice, or _iter_pages re-serves a repeated offset, against a cursor that has already advanced","The new client begins exposing a next_page_token attribute, newly activating _iter_pages' same-token-twice guard on a legitimately repeating final-page token"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"insufficient"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radiu